## Flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## A scheduler that runs out of work spins for a while before it sleeps, which
## takes CPU from libvips threads and, in a container, from its CPU quota. On
## the Performance workflow (2 CPUs), turning off the dirty I/O schedulers'
## spin cut CPU per request by up to 26% in every case family against
## very_short, with requests per second within 5% either way (cache hits at
## two clients 11% faster). The default, short, cost more CPU than
## very_short.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
## libvips runs on dirty CPU schedulers and recurses through an image's whole
## lazy graph when it reads or frees it. ImagePipe bounds that depth, and 8 MB
## stacks (default 320 KB) leave room for anything it misses.
+sssdcpu 1024
## The VM allocates its process table for the process limit at startup: about
## 14 MiB for the default 1,048,576. The server runs one process per open
## connection and a few per request, far fewer than 262,144.
+P 262144
